1
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,700
Excuse me. Can you help me?

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:06,900
Sure, what do you want?

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,400
Where is 83 Wooster Street?

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,900
That's easy. Walk to the corner.

5
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,001
Then make a left turn.

6
00:00:14,001 --> 00:00:16,700
Then walk two blocks to the traffic light.

7
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:18,100
Make another left to Wooster.

8
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,800
Thank you.

9
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:20,900
To the corner and then a left?

10
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:22,400
Yeah. A left.

11
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,800
Hot dog? Only seventy-five cents.

12
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:36,600
No. Thank you. I have a dinner date.

13
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:49,000
555-9470...and it's busy....

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:58,200
Try again.

15
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:08,100
555-9470...and it's still busy.

16
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:09,000
Excuse me, ma'am.

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,600
I'm looking for 83 Wooster Street.

18
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:14,400
Yes. Wooster Street is two blocks,

19
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:20,023
and 83 is to the right, about two houses.

20
00:01:20,023 --> 00:01:21,468
Thank you, thank you!

21
00:01:21,468 --> 00:01:31,100
You're welcome.

22
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:32,200
Who is it?

23
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,792
Harry Bennett. Is this Susan?

24
00:01:33,792 --> 00:01:35,107
Yes, it is. Come up.

25
00:01:35,107 --> 00:01:37,361
I'm on the top floor.

26
00:01:37,361 --> 00:01:39,958
Hello, Harry. It's nice to meet you.

27
00:01:39,958 --> 00:01:41,893
Nice to meet you, Susan.

28
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:43,527
Sorry I'm late.

29
00:01:43,527 --> 00:01:48,618
The traffic. The parking. I was lost.

30
00:01:48,618 --> 00:01:50,261
What pretty flowers! Thank you.

31
00:01:50,261 --> 00:01:52,557
Oh, please come in.

32
00:01:52,557 --> 00:01:55,438
Don't worry about being late. It's fine.

33
00:01:55,438 --> 00:01:58,500
Excuse the mess. I just moved here.

34
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:01,122
Oh, I'd like you to meet my sister-in-law Marilyn.

35
00:02:01,122 --> 00:02:03,221
Marilyn Stewart, this is Harry Bennett.

36
00:02:03,221 --> 00:02:04,300
Pleased to meet you.

37
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,400
Nice to meet you, Harry.

38
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,300
Are we too late for our dinner reservation?

39
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:09,200
No, the restaurant will hold our table.

40
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,066
I know the owner very well.

41
00:02:10,066 --> 00:02:11,500
I eat there a lot.

42
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:12,543
Do you know the phone number of the restaurant?

43
00:02:12,543 --> 00:02:13,700
I'd like to call home

44
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:15,278
and leave the number with the baby-sitter.

45
00:02:15,278 --> 00:02:24,600
Sure. The number is... five five five...seventeen twenty.

46
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:34,200
May I use the phone?

47
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:38,900
Five five five...one seven two oh. Hello?

48
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:40,400
Hi, Michelle. It's Daddy.

49
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,700
Can I speak to Betty?

50
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:46,200
I want to leave the phone number of the restaurant...

51
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:49,700
Hi, Betty. I'll be at five five five...seventeen twenty.

52
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:53,800
OK. Thanks. See you later.

53
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:56,300
Well, that's done. Shall we go?

54
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:58,100
I'm ready. See you later, Marilyn.

55
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:00,000
Have a nice evening.

56
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,200
Bye, Marilyn. Hope to see you again.

57
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:03,300
Me, too. Have fun!

58
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:06,900
Thanks.

59
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:09,900
After you.
